    "created_at": "2016-04-16T16:33:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-16T16:33:59Z",
    "body": "Hey @takenspc!\n\nThis is really interesting. I wonder if, since you want to make changes in this area anyway, we should move to a slightly different strategy.\n\nWhat about this idea?\n- Have wattsi generate two files: link-fixup.js, and fragment-links.json.\n- link-fixup.js contains all the fragment-links data inline (to avoid the second HTTP request) and as JavaScript, not JSON (to avoid the JSON-parsing overhead)\n- link-fixup.js does not wait for DOMContentLoaded\n- link-fixup.js is loaded with a `<script defer>` tag at the top of the file, which should allow the browser to start the HTTP request as soon as possible, but delay execution until all elements on the page are loaded\n\nThis setup seems a bit nicer to me. What do you think?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
